title    Neon Noir
composer Claude (ShooterCoaster)
about    Neon Metropolis (level7) option, round 2 (#1053): a dark sequencer piece in G minor at 152. A metallic FM-bell hook rings over a driving sixteenth saw arpeggio and a galloping synth bass, with rain hissing under the whole loop and a siren far off in the B section. The A section turns Gm-Eb-D (the harmonic minor's F sharp), the B section Cm-Eb-Bb to D7. The last eight bars lift a semitone, to A-flat minor. Layers: hook, arpeggio, bass, rain and siren from the start, then a half-time kick and snare with sixteenth hats at 2x, synth brass doubling the hook an octave down at 3x, open hats and a crash at FRENZY. The helicopter's boss section turns G Phrygian (A flat), chops the bass into rotor sixteenths under a tom and orchestra hits; the sting is G major.
tempo    152
beats    4
steps    4
reverb   0.26

# untagged voices are the base layer, the hook among them (layers only add); the intro plays every layer
voice bell   fmbell   vol=0.6
voice arp    saw      vol=0.2 pan=0.25 gate=0.45
voice bass   synbass  vol=0.62 gate=0.7
voice rain   rain     vol=0.3 pan=-0.2 att=0.08 rel=0.1
voice siren  siren    vol=0.16 pan=-0.5
voice stab   orchhit  vol=0.32 pan=0.1
voice rotor  tommid   vol=0.5 pan=0.15
voice kick   kick     vol=0.75 layer=drums
voice snare  snare    vol=0.6 layer=drums
voice hat    hat      vol=0.3 pan=0.3 layer=drums
voice brass  synbrass vol=0.28 pan=-0.2 layer=lead
voice ohat   ohat909  vol=0.2 pan=-0.35 layer=frenzy
voice crash  crash    vol=0.28 pan=0.2 layer=frenzy

pattern intro
bell  | _ | G5--- D5--- A#5--- A5--- |
brass | _ | G4--- D4--- A#4--- A4--- |
